illions place:.\n\n```.\n  1.\n+ 0.\n-----.\n 14.\n```.\n\nWe write down 4 and carry over 1 to the hundred-millions place.\n\n```.\n  1.\n  1.\n-----.\n 14.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the hundred-millions place:.\n\n```.\n  1.\n+ 8.\n-----.\n 14.\n```.\n\nWe write down 4 and carry over 1 to the billions place.\n\n```.\n  1.\n  1.\n-----.\n 14.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the billions place:.\n\n```.\n  1.\n+ 0.\n-----.\n 14.\n```.\n\nWe write down 4 and carry over 1 to the trillions place.\n\n```.\n  1.\n  1.\n-----.\n 14.\n```.\n\nFinally, we move to the trillions place:.\n\n```.\n  1.\n+ 8.\n-----.\n 14.\n```.\n\nWe write down 4 and carry over 1 to the quadrillions place.\n\n```.\n  1.\n  1.\n-----.\n 14.\n```.\n\nSince there are no more digits to add, we write down the remaining 1 in the quadrillions place.\n\n```.\n  1.\n  1.\n-----.\n 14.\n```.\n\nTherefore, the sum of 824190622 and 203514191 is 1027704813.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
