messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 320935006 and 715664991? Please reason step by step.', "<think>.\nTo find the sum of 320935006 and 715664991, we can use the standard addition algorithm. We start by aligning the numbers by their place values, with the ones place aligned, the tens place aligned, and so on. Then, we add the digits in each column, starting from the rightmost column (the ones place) and moving to the left. If the sum of the digits in a column is greater than 9, we carry over the extra digit to the next column. .\n\nLet's perform the addition step by step:.\n\n```.\n  320935006.\n+ 715664991.\n-----------.\n```.\n\nStarting from the rightmost column (the ones place):.\n\n```.\n  6.\n+ 1.\n-----.\n  7.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the next column (the tens place):.\n\n```.\n  0.\n+ 9.\n-----.\n  9.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the next column (the hundreds place):.\n\n```.\n  0.\n+ 6.\n-----.\n  6.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the next column (the thousands place):.\n\n```.\n  5.\n+ 4.\n-----.\n  9.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the next column (the ten-thousands place):.\n\n```.\n  3.\n+ 6.\n-----.\n  9.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the next column (the hundred-thousands place):.\n\n```.\n  9.\n+ 5.\n-----.\n  14.\n```.\n\nSince 14 is greater than 9, we carry over the extra digit (1) to the next column (the millions place) and write down 4 in the ten-million place:.\n\n```.\n  4.\n+ 1.\n-----.\n  5.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the next column (the hundred-million place):.\n\n```.\n  2.\n+ 1.\n-----.\n  3.\n```.\n\nFinally, we move to the next column (the billion place):.\n\n```.\n  3.\n+ 7.\n-----.\n  10.\n```.\n\nSince 10 is greater than 9, we carry over the extra digit (1) to the next column (the ten-billion place) and write down 0 in the billion place:.\n\n```.\n  0.\n+ 1.\n-----.\n  1.\n```.\n\nNow, we have the final sum:.\n\n```.\n  0.\n+ 1.\n-----.\n  1.\n```.\n\nTherefore, the sum of 320935006 and 715664991 is 1036600000.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
