messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 875916498 and 134101977? Please reason step by step.', "<think>.\nTo find the sum of 875916498 and 134101977, we can use the standard addition algorithm. We start by aligning the numbers by their place values, with the ones place aligned with the ones place, the tens place aligned with the tens place, and so on. Then, we add the digits in each column, starting from the rightmost column (the ones place) and moving to the left. If the sum of the digits in a column is greater than 9, we carry over the extra digit to the next column. .\n\nLet's perform the addition step by step:.\n\n```.\n  875916498.\n+ 134101977.\n-----------.\n```.\n\nStarting from the rightmost column (the ones place):.\n\n```.\n  875916498.\n+ 134101977.\n-----------.\n     5.\n```.\n\nThe sum of the digits in the ones place is 5, so we write 5 in the ones place of the sum.\n\nNext, we move to the next column (the tens place):.\n\n```.\n  875916498.\n+ 134101977.\n-----------.\n    65.\n```.\n\nThe sum of the digits in the tens place is 65, so we write 5 in the tens place of the sum and carry over 6 to the hundreds place.\n\nNext, we move to the next column (the hundreds place):.\n\n```.\n  875916498.\n+ 134101977.\n-----------.\n   656.\n```.\n\nThe sum of the digits in the hundreds place is 656, so we write 6 in the hundreds place of the sum and carry over 6 to the thousands place.\n\nNext, we move to the next column (the thousands place):.\n\n```.\n  875916498.\n+ 134101977.\n-----------.\n  6566.\n```.\n\nThe sum of the digits in the thousands place is 6566, so we write 6 in the thousands place of the sum and carry over 6 to the ten-thousands place.\n\nNext, we move to the next column (the ten-thousands place):.\n\n```.\n  875916498.\n+ 134101977.\n-----------.\n 65666.\n```.\n\nThe sum of the digits in the ten-thousands place is 65666, so we write 6 in the ten-thousands place of the sum and carry over 6 to the hundred-t