messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 810639307 and 482066318? Please reason step by step.', "<think>.\nTo find the sum of 810639307 and 482066318, we can use the standard addition algorithm. We start by aligning the numbers by their place values, with the ones place aligned, the tens place aligned, and so on. Then, we add the digits in each column, starting from the rightmost column (the ones place) and moving to the left. If the sum of the digits in a column is greater than 9, we carry over the extra digit to the next column. .\n\nLet's perform the addition step by step:.\n\n```.\n  810639307.\n+ 482066318.\n-----------.\n```.\n\nStarting from the rightmost column (the ones place):.\n\n```.\n  7.\n+18.\n---.\n 15.\n```.\n\nWe write down 5 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\n```.\n  7.\n+18.\n---.\n 15.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the tens place:.\n\n```.\n 3.\n+6.\n---.\n 9.\n```.\n\nWe write down 9 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\n```.\n 3.\n+6.\n---.\n 9.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the hundreds place:.\n\n```.\n 9.\n+6.\n---.\n15.\n```.\n\nWe write down 5 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\n```.\n 9.\n+6.\n---.\n15.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the thousands place:.\n\n```.\n 3.\n+0.\n---.\n 3.\n```.\n\nWe write down 3 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\n```.\n 3.\n+0.\n---.\n 3.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the ten-thousands place:.\n\n```.\n 9.\n+2.\n---.\n11.\n```.\n\nWe write down 1 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\n```.\n 9.\n+2.\n---.\n11.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the hundred-thousands place:.\n\n```.\n 1.\n+1.\n---.\n 2.\n```.\n\nWe write down 2 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\n```.\n 1.\n+1.\n---.\n 2.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the millions place:.\n\n```.\n 1.\n+0.\n---.\n 1.\n```.\n\nWe write down 1 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\n```.\n 1.\n+0.\n---.\n 1.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the ten-millions place:.\n\n```.\n 1.\n+0.\n---.\n 1.\n```.\n\nWe write down 1 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\n```.\n 1.\n+0.\n---.\n 1.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the hundred-millions place:.\n\n```.\n 1.\n+0.\n---.\n 1.\n```.\n\nWe write down 1 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\n```.\n 1.\n+0.\n---.\n 1.\n```.\n\nFinally, we move to the billion place:.\n\n```.\n 1.\n+0.\n---.\n 1.\n```.\n\nWe write down 1 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\n```.\n 1.\n+0.\n---.\n 1.\n```.\n\nSince there are no more columns to add, we write down the remaining 1 in the billion place.\n\n```.\n 1.\n+0.\n---.\n 1.\n```.\n\nSo, the sum of 810639307 and 482066318 is 1292705625.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
