messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 102261353 and 847144854? Please reason step by step.', "<think>.\nTo find the sum of 102261353 and 847144854, we can use the standard addition algorithm. We start by aligning the numbers by their place values, with the ones place aligned, the tens place aligned, and so on. Then, we add the digits in each column, starting from the rightmost column (the ones place) and moving to the left. If the sum of the digits in a column is greater than 9, we carry over the extra digit to the next column. .\n\nLet's perform the addition step by step:.\n\n```.\n  102261353.\n+ 847144854.\n-----------.\n```.\n\nStarting from the rightmost column (the ones place):.\n\n```.\n3 + 4 = 7.\n```.\n\nMoving to the next column (the tens place):.\n\n```.\n5 + 5 = 10.\n```.\n\nSince 10 is greater than 9, we carry over the extra digit (1) to the next column and write down 0 in the tens place:.\n\n```.\n0.\n```.\n\nContinuing to the next column (the hundreds place):.\n\n```.\n3 + 4 = 7.\n```.\n\nMoving to the next column (the thousands place):.\n\n```.\n1 + 1 = 2.\n```.\n\nContinuing to the next column (the ten-thousands place):.\n\n```.\n2 + 4 = 6.\n```.\n\nContinuing to the next column (the hundred-thousands place):.\n\n```.\n2 + 7 = 9.\n```.\n\nContinuing to the next column (the millions place):.\n\n```.\n0 + 8 = 8.\n```.\n\nContinuing to the next column (the ten-millions place):.\n\n```.\n1 + 4 = 5.\n```.\n\nContinuing to the next column (the hundred-millions place):.\n\n```.\n0 + 4 = 4.\n```.\n\nContinuing to the next column (the billion place):.\n\n```.\n1 + 0 = 1.\n```.\n\nFinally, we have:.\n\n```.\n102261353.\n+ 847144854.\n-----------.\n949406207.\n```.\n\nSo, the sum of 102261353 and 847144854 is 949406207.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
