messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 132845751 and 123968184? Please reason step by step.', "<think>.\nTo find the sum of 132845751 and 123968184, we can use the standard addition algorithm. We start by aligning the numbers by their place values, with the ones place aligned, the tens place aligned, and so on. Then, we add the digits in each column, starting from the rightmost column (the ones place) and moving to the left. If the sum of the digits in a column is greater than 9, we carry over the extra digit to the next column. .\n\nLet's perform the addition step by step:.\n\n```.\n  132845751.\n+ 123968184.\n-----------.\n```.\n\nStarting from the rightmost column (the ones place):.\n\n1 + 4 = 5.\n\nNext column (the tens place):.\n\n5 + 8 = 13. We write down 3 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\nNext column (the hundreds place):.\n\n7 + 1 = 8. We add the carried over 1, which gives us 9.\n\nNext column (the thousands place):.\n\n5 + 6 = 11. We write down 1 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\nNext column (the ten-thousands place):.\n\n4 + 9 = 13. We write down 3 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\nNext column (the hundred-thousands place):.\n\n8 + 3 = 11. We write down 1 and carry over 1 to the next column.\n\nNext column (the millions place):.\n\n2 + 2 = 4. We add the carried over 1, which gives us 5.\n\nNext column (the ten-millions place):.\n\n3 + 1 = 4.\n\nFinally, we have the leftmost column (the hundred-millions place):.\n\n1 + 1 = 2.\n\nPutting it all together, we get:.\n\n```.\n  132845751.\n+ 123968184.\n-----------.\n 256813935.\n```.\n\nSo, the sum of 132845751 and 123968184 is 256813935.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
