21563.\n```.\n\n8. Add the digits in the millions place: 0 + 0 + 1 (carry over) = 1. Write down 1 in the millions place of the sum.\n\n```.\n  904851971.\n+ 700623392.\n----------.\n 11215631.\n```.\n\n9. Add the digits in the ten-millions place: 0 + 0 = 0. Write down 0 in the ten-millions place of the sum.\n\n```.\n  904851971.\n+ 700623392.\n----------.\n 112156310.\n```.\n\n10. Add the digits in the hundred-millions place: 9 + 7 = 16. Write down 6 in the hundred-millions place of the sum and carry over 1 to the billion place.\n\n```.\n  904851971.\n+ 700623392.\n----------.\n 1121563106.\n```.\n\n11. Add the digits in the billion place: 0 + 0 + 1 (carry over) = 1. Write down 1 in the billion place of the sum.\n\n```.\n  904851971.\n+ 700623392.\n----------.\n 11215631016.\n```.\n\nTherefore, the sum of 904851971 and 700623392 is 11215631016.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
