messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 783944466 and 473642303? Please reason step by step.', "<think>.\nTo find the sum of 783944466 and 473642303, we can use the standard addition algorithm. We start by aligning the numbers by their place values, with the ones place aligned, the tens place aligned, and so on. Then, we add the digits in each column, starting from the rightmost column (the ones place) and moving to the left. If the sum of the digits in a column is greater than 9, we carry over the extra digit to the next column. .\n\nLet's perform the addition step by step:.\n\n```.\n  783944466.\n+ 473642303.\n-----------.\n```.\n\nStarting from the rightmost column (the ones place):.\n\n```.\n  6.\n+ 3.\n---.\n  9.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the tens place:.\n\n```.\n  4.\n+ 2.\n---.\n  6.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the hundreds place:.\n\n```.\n  4.\n+ 3.\n---.\n  7.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the thousands place:.\n\n```.\n  4.\n+ 6.\n---.\n  0.\n```.\n\nWe carry over the extra digit (1) to the next column:.\n\n```.\n  4.\n+ 6.\n---.\n  0.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the ten-thousands place:.\n\n```.\n  9.\n+ 3.\n---.\n  2.\n```.\n\nWe carry over the extra digit (1) to the next column:.\n\n```.\n  9.\n+ 3.\n---.\n  2.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the hundred-thousands place:.\n\n```.\n  3.\n+ 7.\n---.\n  0.\n```.\n\nWe carry over the extra digit (1) to the next column:.\n\n```.\n  3.\n+ 7.\n---.\n  0.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the millions place:.\n\n```.\n  8.\n+ 4.\n---.\n  2.\n```.\n\nWe carry over the extra digit (1) to the next column:.\n\n```.\n  8.\n+ 4.\n---.\n  2.\n```.\n\nNext, we move to the ten-millions place:.\n\n```.\n  8.\n+ 4.\n---.\n  2.\n```.\n\nFinally, we move to the hundred-millions place:.\n\n```.\n  7.\n+ 4.\n---.\n  1.\n```.\n\nSo, the sum of 783944466 and 473642303 is 1257586769.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
